      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I'm working on a preliminary assessment for some long-term commercial real estate investments in a few expanding urban districts. We're seeing a lot of rapid demographic shifts in these zones—specifically a high influx of new immigrant populations and changing local compositions. From a risk modeling perspective, what are the key indicators we should be tracking to account for potential social or economic volatility in these neighborhoods? I want to make sure our stability projections are solid.",
