      "content": "While correlation exists, it is critical not to extrapolate generalizations based solely on demographic change; you must rely on localized, real-time data. Instead of applying blanket premiums, weight the risk by the *rate of change* and the *economic correlation* of the shift. A rapid transition coupled with economic gentrification or housing stress tends to correlate with higher instability, so model the friction point between demographic change and affordability gaps. Using localized victimization data provides a much more accurate weighting than relying solely on ethnicity counts.",
