      "content": "Actuarial models and robust urban sociology uniformly caution against using specific ethnic or cultural backgrounds as predictive variables for risk. Blaming generalized backgrounds introduces severe bias and risks discriminatory outcomes. Instead, a sound model should link observable economic and social *conditions*—like high rent burden percentages or low educational attainment across the group—to volatility indicators. Focus your variables on socio-economic stressors and neighborhood strain, rather than immutable group characteristics.",
